 ### BREAKING CHANGES
 
--   `set_epi()`, `record_attr_history()` and `record_raw_object()` have new signatures, with the time step moved last and made optional: `set_epi(dat, item, value, at = NULL)`, `record_attr_history(dat, item, value, at = NULL, posit_ids = NULL, unique_ids = NULL)` and `record_raw_object(dat, label, object, at = NULL)`. `at` defaults to the current time step, `get_current_timestep(dat)`. `record_attr_history()` also renames `attribute` to `item` and `values` to `value`. Since a call in the old argument order would silently record the time step as the value, `at`, `posit_ids` and `unique_ids` must now be passed by name, and an old positional call such as `set_epi(dat, "i.num", at, value)` stops with an error that gives the new signature. Code that must run on both 2.6.x and 2.7.0 can pass `at` and `posit_ids` by name and the other arguments by position, as in `set_epi(dat, "i.num", value, at = at)`; the renamed arguments of `record_attr_history()` cannot be passed by name on both (#1006, #1007).
