--   Fix scenarios that set some positions of a vector parameter. A scenario column with a position suffix now sets only that position of the current value, in `use_scenario()` and in updaters; it used to replace the whole vector, so a scenario setting only `prep.start.rate_1 = 0.5` turned `prep.start.rate = c(0.0055, 0.0042, 0.0066)` into `0.5` rather than `c(0.5, 0.0042, 0.0066)`. A column without a suffix still replaces the whole parameter. Positions past the end of the vector extend it when they leave no gap and are an error otherwise, suffixed columns can no longer shorten a vector, and setting by position a parameter that is not a plain vector (a `multilayer()` or `by_infection_duration()` object, or a list) is an error.
